<title>USA: Apple eyes selling Sun Newton-paper.</title>
<headline>Apple eyes selling Sun Newton-paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer and Sun Microsystems are in talks over possibly selling Apple's Newton unit to Sun, USA Today said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Sun could be a tough sell and no deal was imminent. Talks appeared centered on Newton and Sun's programming language Java, it said.</p>
<p>Newton is the operating system for Apple's hand-held MessagePad computer and its eMate portable computer for children, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The unit has yet to make money, USA Today said.</p>
<p>Neither company was immediately available to comment on the report.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
